==English==

===Alternative forms===
This expression is frequently seen as
* '''pulling teeth'''
* '''like pulling teeth'''

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-pull teeth.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|dentistry}} To [[extract]] teeth, usually due to [[disease]] or [[damage]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[perform]] an [[action]] or [[task]] that is especially [[difficult]] or [[effortful]].
#: {{syn|en|get blood out of a stone}}
#: {{ux|en|You will probably have to '''pull teeth''' to get a straight answer from a car salesman.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022-10-07|author=Emma Goldberg|title=The Job Market Has Been Like Musical Chairs. Will the Music Stop?|journal={{w|The New York Times}}|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/07/business/job-market-tightening.html|passage=“We thought there would be a mad rush of students participating in these events, and it was like '''pulling teeth''' to get students to come out,” she recalled.}}

